$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Amides
34a-l. A mixture of 33 (33 mg, 0.10 mmol) and 1-hydroxybenzotriazole
(18.9 mg, 0.14 mmol) in DMF (0.5 mL) was shaken for 15 min.
N-Methylmorpholine (44 μL, 0.40 mmol) was added followed by the
corresponding benzylamine (0.12 mmol) in DMF (0.5 mL).
1-Ethyl-3-(3′-dimethylaminopropyl)carbodiimide hydrochloride (26.8 mg,
0.14 mmol) was then added, and the mixture was shaken for 18 h. The
reaction mixture was purified by reverse phase preparative HPLC to afford
the title compound.
N-(3,4-Difluorobenzyl)-4-(2-(((trans)-4-(hydroxymethyl)-cyclohexyl)methyl)-2H-tetrazol-5-yl)-6-methylpicolinamide
(34g). 74% yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 9.36 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 1 H),
8.38 (s, 1 H), 8.05 (s, 1 H), 7.39-7.30 (m, 2 H), 7.13-7.18 (m, 1 H),
4.62 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2 H), 4.47 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 2 H), 4.32 (t, J = 5.3
Hz, 1 H), 3.14 (t, J = 5.9 Hz, 2 H), 2.64 (s, 3 H), 1.97-1.87 (m, 1 H),
1.70 (d, J = 11.0 Hz, 2 H), 1.57 (d, J = 12.1 Hz, 2 H), 1.30-1.18 (m, 1
H), 1.03 (q, J = 12.8 Hz, 2 H), 0.83 (q, J = 11.3 Hz, 2 H). MS (ES+) m/z
457 (M + H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
N-(4-Fluoro-3-methoxybenzyl)-6-(2-(((2S,5R)-5-(hydroxymethyl)-1,4-dioxan-2-yl)methyl)-2H-tetrazol-5-yl)-2-methylpyrimidine-4-carboxamide.
A Highly Selective and Orally Bioavailable Matrix Metalloproteinase-13
Inhibitor for the Potential Treatment of Osteoarthritis
